nts/3198662819","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/2512#issuecomment-3198662819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/2512","id":3198662819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6-p7ij","user":{"login":"oliviertassinari","id":3165635,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjU2MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3165635?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari","html_url":"https://github.com/oliviertassinari","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T22:56:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T22:27:58Z","body":"The a11y of this component seems a bit buggy:\n\n- [ ] 1. When using the keyboard modality, the focus-visible style doesn't show:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b39a7e37-c1e3-468e-88c1-737065e36050\n\nSame bug in https://joy-ui.com/slider/. But in https://react-spectrum.adobe.com/react-aria/Slider.html or https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/input/range it's correct.\n\n- [ ] 2. When you focus the slider with a keyboard (focusing the div), and you change the value, VoiceOver doesn't announce value changes. Probably same bug as 1.\n- [ ] 3. #2545\n- [ ] 4. There is a `role: 'group'`, I don't understand why it's here for a single slider. VoiceOver announces it. Is this for the range slider only?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3198662819/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3218763976","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/2512#issuecomment-3218763976","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/2512","id":3218763976,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6_2nDI","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-25T04:08:42Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T04:08:42Z","body":"> Is it intended that slider thumb is two focusable elements?\n\nWe found it's intentional that the `input` must receive focus in order to support Android Talkback: https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/2537#issuecomment-3218335240\n\nRA's slider ([sandbox](https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/react-aria-slider-forked-3l4rmy)) 